9-dd00-524e-9906-ac4f9a9f0e84" :question/math-academy-id "q-71835" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=8$, $|\\,q\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Find the vector projection of $p$ onto $q$ in terms of the vector $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =|\\,p\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $q:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{q}{|\\,q\\,|}=\\frac{q}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}q\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,p & ={\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p\\cdot u \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}q \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}q\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19220/selection/736a609de9e9ce01f5cd38aae8e843a8dac54af69441f71cadc69d6dfe39ea58" :answer/id #uuid "172c5ba2-541e-5ce0-8c73-13f6018d1640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{2}b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19220/selection/956130ea6ab6297ca966bb60b519ee723f070e91760ae4af327f037bb50fc269" :answer/id #uuid "ab256ca4-7de4-52c8-ace1-038bf415592a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19220/selection/80f28cffca9c209ac5beb01e805e57b7be541c4a68029bc4ae89a5d0a5a4106d" :answer/id #uuid "a1303fc3-54c1-5760-9384-5e0c7e0cba79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\sqrt{2}b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19220/selection/ca7cacdb43eea79509524cf4971850c6b449f0d4698782541facb03ea679051d" :answer/id #uu